{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep — you.</b> You are the ones who keep — you opened first. And so it says: ״גן נעול אחותי כלה״ (A locked garden is my sister, my bride)." "<b>Et my statutes.</b> The section of forbidden relations that I mentioned." "<b>And my ordinances.</b> That you shall carry out the judgment that I command upon one who transgresses any one of them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The phrase 'אתם שומרים שאתם פתחתם תחלה' is elliptical; rendered hyper-literally. The connection to the Song of Songs quotation appears to be through the wordplay of guarding/locking."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:17.776848455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}